    "observed": "BothOS terminal matrix returned Starting with TimedOut status already published; Ubuntu genuine-Lost case also observed active. Other new tests passed.",
    "assessment": "Inspection source returns the original active state only when live_lock reports held. Thus close-only fixture release did not establish required absence. Concurrent subprocess fork inheritance of flock-backed descriptors is plausible from source, not instrumented to a particular child.",
    "fix": "Test-only explicit FileExt::unlock before dropping the actual owner establishes fixture ownership release across inherited descriptors. Genuine-Lost test uses a single public inspection to avoid duplicate absence probes. No production wait/retry/seam revision or assertion suppression."
  },
  "findings_and_fixes": [
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "finding": "Status read can observe Starting/Running before terminal publication, then observe the released liveness lock and incorrectly return Lost from its stale snapshot.",
      "fix": "Only after first active plus absent lock, reread existing bounded status once; latest active remains genericLost, latest terminal or storedLost returned unchanged; all read/lock errors propagate."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2 test fixture",
      "finding": "Dropping a fixture File does not guarantee flock release if fork-inherited duplicate descriptors remain; repeated absence queries can also create new transient lock observations.",
      "fix": "Explicit fixture unlock and one genuine-Lost observation; retained failed validation and source review before requalification."
    }
  ],
